<title>INDIA: Indian soy market prices rise, local demand low.</title>
<headline>Indian soy market prices rise, local demand low.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices rose on Monday in plant delivery condition by 100 rupees per tonne, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were steady in central Indian markets with arrivals around 20,000 tonnes. Undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down by 200 rupees per tonne on increased supply from plants and refineries. Local market demand was low on poor volumes.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady on strong prices level. Soymeal yellow was $275-276 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $130 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,450 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,400-4,425 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
